            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0536" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/1128: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-22T11:00:00+02:00">June 22, 1943—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 22—10:04 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1372. Legation’s 1303, June 12, 6 p.m. Notes have been exchanged extending the
                    wolfram agreement from March 1 to June 30, 1943, with clause (G) modified by the
                    raising of the Anglo-American off-take from the pool to 50 percent. Copies by
                    pouch.</p>
                <p>Repeated to London and Madrid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
